{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Policy - Rule - Okta Policy Rule Modified or Deleted",
	"Description": "A rule inside an Okta policy was modified or deleted. Policy rules are where the actual conditions live, so an adversary can leave the policy in place and still neutralise it by editing or removing the rule that enforces MFA.\n\nEvent types: policy.rule.update, policy.rule.delete\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_policy_rule_modified_or_deleted/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/okta_policy_rule_modified_or_deleted.yml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
